Part 3: input methods, selectWeapon/toggleBuild/setBuildType, pointer mapping.

```
  onKeyDown(e) {
    const k = e.key.toLowerCase();
    if (this.state === 'menu') { if (k==='enter'||k===' ') { e.preventDefault(); this.startMatch(); } return; }
    if (this.state === 'over') { if (k==='enter'||k==='r') this.startMatch(); return; }
    if (['arrowleft','arrowright','arrowup','arrowdown',' '].includes(k)) e.preventDefault();
    if (k==='a'||k==='arrowleft') this.keys.left=true;
    ...
    if (k==='w'||k==='arrowup') this.keys.up=true;
    ...
    if (k===' ' && !e.repeat) this.jump();
    if (k==='enter' && !e.repeat) { this.sound.unlock(); fire(this); }
    if (['1','2','3'].includes(k)) this.selectWeapon(Number(k)-1);
    if (k==='b' && !e.repeat) this.toggleBuild();
    if (k==='escape') { this.buildMode=false; this.drag=null; this.updateHud(true); }
    if (k==='r' && !e.repeat) { this.rampDir *= -1; if(this.buildType==='ramp') this.toast('RAMP FLIPPED'); this.updateHud(true);}
  }
```
Careful: `e.key` for space is ' '; `.toLowerCase()` fine.

Need prevent space page scroll. `e.preventDefault()` for space always.

Pointer:
```
  onPointerDown(e) {
    this.sound.unlock();
    if (e.button !== undefined && e.button !== 0 && e.pointerType==='mouse') return;
    const p = this.toWorld(e);
    this.pointer = p;
    if (this.state !== 'aim') return;
    if (this.buildMode) {
      if (this.dom.rotateHint && !hidden?) no
      this.placeCurrentBuild(p);
      return;
    }
    this.drag = { id: e.pointerId, sx: p.x, sy: p.y, moved: 0 };
    try { this.canvas.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); } catch {}
    this.aimFromPoint(p);
  }
```
Need not start drag if pointerdown on HUD; canvas only.

`onPointerMove`:
```
const p=toWorld; this.pointer=p;
if (this.drag && this.drag.id===e.pointerId) {
 const d=Math.hypot(p.x-this.drag.sx,p.y-this.drag.sy);
 this.drag.moved=Math.max(this.drag.moved,d);
 if (this.drag.moved>4) this.aimFromPoint(p);
}
```
`onPointerUp`:
```
if (this.drag && drag.id===...) { const moved=drag.moved; this.drag=null; if (moved>10 && state==='aim' && !buildMode) { fire(this); } }
```
`aimFromPoint`:
```
const w=this.active; if(!w) return;
const dx=p.x-w.x, dy=p.y-w.y;
const d=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
if (d < 10) return;
let ang = Math.atan2(-dy,dx)*180/PI;
ang = clamp(ang, 3, 177);
this.aim.angle = ang;
this.aim.power = clamp((d-20)/5.0, 5, 100);
```
Hmm if pointer left/below, atan2(-negative, negative) → third quadrant angle ~ -135 -> clamp 3. Fine.

`toWorld(e)`:
```
const rect = this.canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
return { x:(e.clientX-rect.left)/this.view.scale + this.camX, y:(e.clientY-rect.top)/this.view.scale + this.camY };
```

`placeCurrentBuild(p)`:
```
if (!this.active) return;
const ok = placeBuild(this, this.buildType, p.x, p.y, 0, false);
if (ok) { this.buildPreview=null; }
```
Build mode stays.

`selectWeapon(i)`:
```
if (i<0||i>=WEAPONS.length) return;
const w=this.active;
if (this.state!=='aim' || !w) return;
if ((w.ammo[WEAPONS[i].id]??0)<=0 && i!==0) { this.toast('OUT OF AMMO'); this.sound.invalid(); return; }
this.selectedWeapon=i;
this.buildMode=false;
this.sound.select();
this.updateHud(true);
```
Even when out of ammo for i=0? rocket infinite. fine.

`toggleBuild(force)`:
```
if (this.state!=='aim') return;
this.buildMode = force===undefined ? !this.buildMode : force;
this.drag=null;
if (this.buildMode) { this.buildType = this.buildType || 'wall'; this.showBanner('BUILD MODE', 'gold', 700); }
else { this.showBanner('WEAPONS READY', '', 600); }
this.sound.select();
this.updateHud(true);
```
But startTurn resets buildMode; okay.

`setBuildType(type)`: validate; set buildMode true, buildType; sound; updateHud.

`updateTargetChip` and HUD later.

Part 3 also helpers: `onKeyUp`, `clearKeys`.

Let's append.

