Now update visuals drawScreenOverlay to use vignette cache if present, and maybe draw clouds separately? World bg cached includes static clouds.

Modify:
```
if (g.vignetteCache) drawImage
else gradient.
```

Then Game: add caches, render changes, loop pause.

Add in setupWorld:
```
this.worldBg = null; this.skyCache=null; this.vignetteCache=null; this.cacheKey='';
```
Actually sky/vignette can persist across matches; reset on resize only. But setupWorld recreates clouds; worldBg must reset. Add `this.worldBg=null`.

Add method `ensureCaches()`:
```
const {cw,ch,dpr}=this.view;
const key=`${cw}x${ch}@${dpr}`;
if (this.cacheKey!==key) {
 this.skyCache=document.createElement('canvas'); width=cw;height=ch;
 drawScreenSky(skyCtx, {view:this.view}) // drawScreenSky uses g.view only, fine.
 this.vignetteCache=canvas cw,ch; radial gradient...
 this.cacheKey=key;
}
if (!this.worldBg) {
 const c=document.createElement('canvas'); c.width=W;c.height=H;
 const bgCtx=c.getContext('2d');
 drawWorldBackground(bgCtx,this);
 this.worldBg=c;
}
```
`drawScreenSky(ctx, this)` uses `g.view` and works.

World background caching uses `g.clouds` and `g.time`; draw once.

Vignette: replicate drawScreenOverlay's gradient. Or call drawScreenOverlay into vignette canvas? That includes motes and flash—no. Just gradient.

Render:
```
drawScreenSky? replace with drawImage(this.skyCache,0,0,cw,ch)
...
ctx.drawImage(this.worldBg,0,0)
...
drawScreenOverlay (uses cache)
```
Ensure caches before drawing.

Loop pause:
```
loop(now) {
 if (!this.running) return;
 ...
 this.update(dt); this.render();
 if (this.state==='menu') { this.running=false; this.lastTime=0?; return; }
 this.raf = requestAnimationFrame(this.loop);
}
startLoop(){ if (this.running) return; this.running=true; this.lastTime=0; this.raf=requestAnimationFrame(this.loop); }
```
But constructor calls requestAnimationFrame(this.loop) directly; set running=true before. When menu first frame renders, sets running=false and stops. After startMatch: call startLoop. Also when state over? keep running to animate ghosts and result overlay; could stop after 3s but not needed.

Need ensure if Play is clicked before first frame rendered (unlikely), loop stops after rendering game? startMatch starts loop. The initial RAF may fire after click; state aim so keeps going.

Implement:
- constructor: `this.running = true; this.raf = null; this.loop = this.loop.bind(this); requestAnimationFrame(this.loop);`
- loop: if state menu after render: running=false; return (no schedule). On startMatch: `this.lastTime = 0;` and if !running: running=true; requestAnimationFrame(loop). But if the menu loop still scheduled? We stop scheduling. If startMatch called while loop is in-flight? event happens between frames; running false; startLoop sets true; fine.
- Need avoid duplicate RAF: set `this.raf` and maybe cancel? We only schedule when running; after stop, no pending. startLoop schedules.
- On game over, maybe stop after result? We can keep loop. Fine.

Also `lastTime` handling: loop sets if !lastTime. After pause, set lastTime=0 in startLoop so dt=0 on first frame.

Additionally, in `endMatch`, keep running. Good.

Now update game.js edits.

